   "text": "I read the structure in five parts and wrote the SMILES from them.\n\n1. **Hydantoin:** an imidazolidine-2,4-dione ring with an exocyclic C=CH at C5. On the drawing, the ring NH and the aryl group sit on the same side of the double bond. The NH outranks the C=O carbon on C5, and the aryl group outranks H on the CH, so this is Z.\n2. **Phenyl ring:** meta-disubstituted, carrying the CH= at one position and the quaternary carbon at the other.\n3. **Quaternary carbon:** bears a methyl, the phenyl, the triazole C3, and a chain of three CH2, then C(CH3)2, then CH2, then SO2, then CH2CH2. That chain ends on C4 of the indole.\n4. **Indole:** C4 carries the chain, C5 carries the ring oxygen, C6 carries F, and C7 is CH. The NH is free.\n5. **Aryl\u2013triazole part:** a 1-methyl-1,2,4-triazole joins the quaternary carbon (at C3) to a fluorophenyl ring (at C5). On that ring, F is ortho to the triazole attachment, and the aryl ether oxygen is meta to the triazole attachment and para to F.\n\nI counted three CH2 groups between the quaternary carbon and the CMe2 from the drawing, which is the least certain count.\n\nSMILES: O=C1NC(=O)/C(=C\\c2cccc(c2)C3(C)CCCC(C)(C)CS(=O)(=O)CCc4c5cc[nH]c5cc(F)c4Oc6ccc(F)c(c6)-c7nc3nn7C)N1\n\nI did not assign any stereo to the quaternary carbon, since it is drawn with plain bonds.\n\nSMILES: O=C1NC(=O)/C(=C/c2cccc(c2)C3(C)CCCC(C)(C)CS(=O)(=O)CCc4c5cc[nH]c5cc(F)c4Oc6ccc(F)c(c6)-c7nc3nn7C)N1"
